LPC2129 I2C Registers
---------------------

1. I2CONSET
2. I2STAT
3. I2DAT
4. I2ADR
5. I2SCLH
6. I2SCLL
7. I2CONCLR 

I2C Bit Frequency Settings
--------------------------

Software must set values for registers I2SCLH and I2SCLL to select the appropriate data rate.

	Bit frequency = FCLK / (I2SCLL + I2SCLH)

	Where FCLK - Frequency of PCLK 

	Bit frequency = PCLK / (I2SCLL + I2SCLH)

	100 Kbps = 15 MHZ / (I2SCLL + I2SCLH)

	I2SCLL + I2SCLH = 15000000 / 100000 

			I2SCLL = 75; // for 100 Kbps 
			I2SCLH = 75; // for 100 Kbps 


I2C Operating Modes
-------------------

	1. Master write 
	2. Master read
	3. Slave write  	 
	4. Slave read  

		slave write and slave read are only used in multi master communication 

	
	    +--------------+        +---------------+
        |      M1      |        |       M2      |
        | (Master mode)|        |  (slave mode) |
        +--------------+        +---------------+
                |                        |
                |                        |
                |                        |
                |                        |
        ------------------------------------------- I2C Bus
                   |               |
                   |               |
                   |               |
                 +----+          +----+
                 | S1 |          | S2 |
                 +----+          +----+
                  0xA0            0xB0


	If M2 is operating in slave mode, it must be assigned a slave address by the programmer so that the master can communicate with it.






















		
